1.23.m:
Then too, I shall become known by name as Guhāvāsin,
on the peak of the Himavat, the very lofty Mahālaya;
Mahālaya will become a most sacred field of perfection.

1.25.m:
Understand how the Lord gave himself in the form of sonship;
when the conflict with Madhu and Kaiṭabha along with Viṣṇu and Jiṣṇu was ended,
Brahmā spoke to Viṣṇu:

1.28.m:
Saṃhūti gave birth to the lord Parjanya, the son of Agni.
Hiraṇyaroman generated Parjanya upon Mārīcī;
he is remembered as the guardian of the world who endures until the dissolution of all beings.

In Prīti, wife of Pulastya, Dattāli was born as her son;
he is remembered as Agastya in a previous birth in the cosmic age of Svāyambhuva Manu.
The middle one was Devabāhu, and Vinīta—these were the three.

To Kratu, auspicious offspring equal to Kratu were born;
they have neither wife nor son, for all of them are celibate.
They are celebrated as sixty thousand Vālakhilyas.
